IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nd-pit`

-- North Dakota Century Code chapter 57-38 -- the individual taxpayer's questions. Every question calls the rules in
-- nd-pit.l4; nothing is restated here. Federal amounts come from the person's federal return.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Am I a North Dakota resident`

@export Am I a North Dakota resident for income tax under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-01(11)?
GIVEN `I am domiciled in North Dakota` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether North Dakota is your domicile (your permanent home, the place you intend to return to)
      `I keep a permanent place of abode in North Dakota` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a permanent place to live in North Dakota
      `months I spent in North Dakota` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of the year, in total, you spent in North Dakota
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a North Dakota resident` IF
    `is a resident` `I am domiciled in North Dakota` `I keep a permanent place of abode in North Dakota` `months I spent in North Dakota`

§ `Must I file, and by when`

@export Must I file a North Dakota income tax return under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-31(1)?
GIVEN `I am a North Dakota resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a North Dakota resident (see the residence question)
      `I must file a federal return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Internal Revenue Code requires you to file a federal income tax return for the year
      `I have income from North Dakota sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received income derived from sources in North Dakota (for example wages for work done in North Dakota), whether or not you are a resident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file a North Dakota return` IF
    `must file a North Dakota return under s 57-38-31(1)` `I am a North Dakota resident` `I must file a federal return` `I have income from North Dakota sources`

@export By what date must I file my calendar-year North Dakota return and pay the tax under N.D.C.C. ss 57-38-34(2) and 57-38-35?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar tax year, for example 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file and pay` MEANS `the due date for a calendar-year return` `the tax year`

-- Only if the IRS changed your federal return, or you amended it.
@export If my federal taxable income was changed by the IRS or I amended my federal return, by what date must I tell North Dakota under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-34.4?
GIVEN `the date of the final determination or of my amended federal return` IS A DATE @desc The date the IRS change became final, or the date you filed your amended federal return
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report a federal change` MEANS
    `the last day to report a federal change` `the date of the final determination or of my amended federal return`

§ `My North Dakota taxable income`

@export What is my North Dakota taxable income under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-30.3(2)?
GIVEN `my federal taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal taxable income on your federal return, in US dollars
      `my US bond interest and other federally exempt income` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest on US government obligations and other income exempt from state tax by federal law or the constitutions, included in federal taxable income, in US dollars
      `my net long-term capital gain` IS A NUMBER @desc Net long-term capital gain over net short-term capital loss, to the extent allocated to North Dakota, in US dollars
      `my qualified dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc Qualified dividends taxed federally at the lower capital gain rates, to the extent allocated to North Dakota, in US dollars
      `my averaged lump sum distribution` IS A NUMBER @desc A lump sum distribution for which you elected federal income averaging under IRC s 402, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my military pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Pay as a member of the armed forces on federal active duty, the national guard or the reserves, included in taxable income, in US dollars
      `my military retirement benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc Retired military personnel benefits received, in US dollars
      `my taxable social security` IS A NUMBER @desc Social security benefits included in your federal AGI under IRC s 86, in US dollars
      `my other North Dakota reductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other reductions under s 57-38-30.3(2), in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my other North Dakota increases` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other increases under s 57-38-30.3(2), in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my North Dakota taxable income` MEANS
    `North Dakota taxable income` `my federal taxable income` `my US bond interest and other federally exempt income` (`the s 57-38-30.3(2)(d) reduction` `my net long-term capital gain` `my qualified dividends`) `my averaged lump sum distribution` `my military pay` `my military retirement benefits` `my taxable social security` `my other North Dakota reductions` `my other North Dakota increases`

§ `My North Dakota tax`

@export How much North Dakota income tax is due on my North Dakota taxable income under the rate schedule printed in N.D.C.C. s 57-38-30.3(1)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your federal filing status: single, married filing jointly, surviving spouse, married filing separately, or head of household
      `I was a resident for the whole year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a North Dakota resident for the entire year (part-year and nonresidents are not covered)
      `my North Dakota taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your North Dakota taxable income (see the taxable income question), in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much North Dakota tax on the printed schedule` MEANS
    `the s 57-38-30.3 tax` `I was a resident for the whole year` `my North Dakota taxable income` (`the schedule in the Century Code` `my filing status`)

@export How much North Dakota income tax is due under the indexed schedule the Tax Commissioner prescribed for the year under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-30.3(1)(g)?
GIVEN `I was a resident for the whole year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a North Dakota resident for the entire year
      `my North Dakota taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your North Dakota taxable income, in US dollars
      `where the 1.95% rate starts` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable income above which 1.95% applies, from the Tax Commissioner's schedule for your filing status and year (the Century Code's figure is $44,725 single, $74,750 joint or surviving spouse, $37,375 married separately, $59,950 head of household)
      `where the 2.50% rate starts` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable income above which 2.50% applies, from the same schedule (the Century Code's figure is $225,975 single, $275,100 joint or surviving spouse, $137,550 married separately, $250,550 head of household)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much North Dakota tax on the indexed schedule` MEANS
    `the s 57-38-30.3 tax` `I was a resident for the whole year` `my North Dakota taxable income` (`schedule` `where the 1.95% rate starts` `where the 2.50% rate starts`)

-- Only for a married couple filing jointly.
@export How much is our North Dakota marriage penalty credit as a married couple filing jointly, under N.D.C.C. s 57-38-01.28, on the schedules printed in the Century Code?
GIVEN `our joint North Dakota taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your joint North Dakota taxable income, in US dollars
      `the lower-earning spouse's qualifying income` IS A NUMBER @desc The earned income (IRC s 32(c)(2)) plus pension and annuity income, included in North Dakota taxable income, of the spouse with less of it, in US dollars
      `the federal exemption amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of one personal exemption under IRC s 151(d) for the year, in US dollars (0 while the federal exemption amount is zero)
      `the federal basic standard deduction for a joint return` IS A NUMBER @desc The basic standard deduction for a joint return under IRC s 63(c)(2)(A) for the year, in US dollars
      `the maximum credit for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum credit as adjusted by the Tax Commissioner for the year ($300 in the Century Code), in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is our marriage penalty credit` MEANS
    `the marriage penalty credit` `our joint North Dakota taxable income` `the lower-earning spouse's qualifying income` `the federal exemption amount` `the federal basic standard deduction for a joint return` `the maximum credit for the year` (`the schedule in the Century Code` `married filing jointly`) (`the schedule in the Century Code` `single`)
